{"step_index":140,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:40:53Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Walkthrough of authentic photos update and the new MAD Explorer Passport unlock gamification.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Walkthrough: Authentic Photos & MAD Tourist Explorer Passport Unlock Experience\n\nThe Jharkhand Tourism platform has been supercharged with **100% authentic verified photographs** from Wikimedia Commons and a **MAD Gamified Tourist Passport Unlock System** where tourists unlock official destination stamps and rank up as they explore!\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 Key Additions & Changes\n\n### 1. 📸 100% Authentic Photos of Famous Places\nAll placeholder images have been replaced with real, verified, high-resolution photographs from Wikimedia Commons:\n- **Hundru Falls**: Real 98m cascade dropping on basalt rocks in Ranchi.\n- **Patratu Valley & Dam**: Authentic twilight view of the winding 30 hairpin ribbon roads and reservoir.\n- **Baba Baidyanath Dham**: Genuine view of the 72-foot stone spire with rare Panchasula in Deoghar.\n- **Parasnath Hill (Shikharji)**: Actual panoramic vista of the Anantnatha Tonk along the sacred ridge.\n- **Betla National Park**: Entrance gate and Sal forest landscape.\n- **Dassam Falls**: Real photography of the Kanchi river cascade.\n- **Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)**: True hanging valley waterfall.\n- **Netarhat**: The pine plantations and mist of the Queen of Chotanagpur.\n- **Lodh Falls (Burha Ghaag)**: 143-meter multi-tiered giant in Latehar.\n- **Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary**: Hilltop elephant sanctuary overlook.\n- **Tagore Hill (Morabadi)**: Shanti Dham stone pavilion atop the granite hill.\n- **Maithon Dam & Lake**: The blue water reservoir and green islands.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 🎒 The MAD \"Tourist Explorer Passport\" Unlock Experience\nThe website now functions like an **interactive discovery expedition**:\n- **Live Progress Counter**: `[🎒 Passport: 0/12 Unlocked]` sits in the navigation and updates in real-time.\n- **How Tourists Unlock Places**:\n  1. Hovering over any destination card for $\\ge 1.2\\text{s}$ triggers the unlock.\n  2. Clicking \"Explore Details\" or \"View on Map\" automatically stamps that destination.\n  3. Clicking any marker pin on the Leaflet Map unlocks that location.\n- **Cinematic Golden Unlock Celebration**:\n  - **Canvas Confetti & Gold Sparkle Shower**: A particle burst cascades down the screen.\n  - **Toast Notification**: *\"Passport Stamp Collected: [Place Name]! +150 XP\"*.\n  - **Card Seal Upgrade**: The card transforms with a glowing gold/emerald badge: `🏆 Stamp Collected`.\n- **Digital Leather & Gold Explorer Passport Modal**:\n  - Click the **\"🎒 Passport\"** button to open the digital passport book.\n  - See your 12 collectible stamp slots (unlocked places show real photos with official seal, while locked places show mysterious silhouettes with adventure clues!).\n  - Earn Traveler Ranks: **Novice Tourist** $\\to$ **Forest Wanderer** $\\to$ **Plateau Trailblazer** $\\to$ **Grand Master of Jharkhand 👑**.\n  - Includes a **\"✨ Unlock All Stamps (Demo Mode)\"** button to test the full 12/12 unlocked state immediately!\n\n---\n\n### 3. 🔇 Removed Nature Audio Section\n- Completely removed the nature audio synthesizer and button from the navigation and JavaScript as requested.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Experience It Live\n\nOpen in your browser:\n👉 **[http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)**\n","Description":"Update walkthrough artifact with authentic pictures and gamified passport details","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Bhavish Sawant\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\22b254db-894b-457d-9362-6954f3cf5219\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Updating walkthrough artifact","toolSummary":"Updating walkthrough artifact"}}]}
